Subject: MIPS: PCI: octeon: don't free octeon_pci_pcibios_map_irq after init

It is reached via pcibios_map_irq() -> pci_assign_irq() whenever a PCI driver
probes; for modular drivers (ath9k on D-Link DSR-1000N) that is after init
memory is freed, so the call jumps into freed .init.text and oopses.

--- a/arch/mips/pci/pci-octeon.c	2026-11-10 18:18:16.080283063 +1100
+++ b/arch/mips/pci/pci-octeon.c	2026-11-10 18:18:16.083017022 +1100
@@ -231,7 +231,7 @@
  *		 as it goes through each bridge.
  * Returns Interrupt number for the device
  */
-int __init octeon_pci_pcibios_map_irq(const struct pci_dev *dev,
+int octeon_pci_pcibios_map_irq(const struct pci_dev *dev,
 				      u8 slot, u8 pin)
 {
 	int irq_num;
